#: ../pwntools/docs/source/term.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.term` --- Terminal handling"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.term.can_init:1
msgid ""
"This function returns True iff stderr is a TTY and we are not inside a "
"REPL.  Iff this function returns `True`, a call to :meth:`init` will let "
"``pwnlib`` manage the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.term.init:1
msgid ""
"Calling this function will take over the terminal (iff :func:`can_init` "
"returns True) until the current python interpreter is closed."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.term.init:4
msgid ""
"It is on our TODO, to create a function to \"give back\" the terminal "
"without closing the interpreter."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.term.term_mode:1
msgid ""
"This is True exactly when we have taken over the terminal using "
":func:`init`."
msgstr ""

